what is git and github?
git is a distributed version control system used to track changes in the source code, maintain version history,and develop new features independently using branches.github is a platform used to host the repositories and colaborate with other developers.

diff b/w normal directory and git repo?
Normal directory
it contains folders and files
doesn't track the file changes 
doesn't maintain the commit history

Git Repo
stores your project files and folders
Contains a hidden .git directory.
Tracks changes when you stage and commit them
maintain the commit history

diff b/w stage / local and remote?
local = working directory
This is where u create and edit your project files 

staging :
This is where you select the changes you want to include in your next commit.
git add . 
git add <filename>
 
Remote Repository:
this is repository, host on remote server such as git hub, where you share your committed code.
Command: git push 

